00/image/jaoe38c1mb1ni3q0/be8fc52f-524d-45b8-a621-14a352e4c9e5/7ad38d80-384c-11f0-aca4-dfd8c6b21521/file-jaoe38c1mb1ni3q1.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mb1niacu/f33b4b80-184a-42eb-afc8-8744b71d525d/7ff380e0-384c-11f0-aca4-dfd8c6b21521/file-jaoe38c1mb1niacv.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mb1niacu/f33b4b80-184a-42eb-afc8-8744b71d525d/7ff380e0-384c-11f0-aca4-dfd8c6b21521/file-jaoe38c1mb1niacv.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2025 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Hydrocarbons Question 5 English Option 4\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1mb1niacu/f33b4b80-184a-42eb-afc8-8744b71d525d/7ff380e0-384c-11f0-aca4-dfd8c6b21521/file-jaoe38c1mb1niacv.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1mb1niacu/f33b4b80-184a-42eb-afc8-8744b71d525d/7ff380e0-384c-11f0-aca4-dfd8c6b21521/file-jaoe38c1mb1niacv.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mb1niacu/f33b4b80-184a-42eb-afc8-8744b71d525d/7ff380e0-384c-11f0-aca4-dfd8c6b21521/file-jaoe38c1mb1niacv.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1mb1niacu/f33b4b80-184a-42eb-afc8-8744b71d525d/7ff380e0-384c-11f0-aca4-dfd8c6b21521/file-jaoe38c1mb1niacv.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1mb1niacu/f33b4b80-184a-42eb-afc8-8744b71d525d/7ff380e0-384c-11f0-aca4-dfd8c6b21521/file-jaoe38c1mb1niacv.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1mb1niacu/f33b4b80-184a-42eb-afc8-8744b71d525d/7ff380e0-384c-11f0-aca4-dfd8c6b21521/file-jaoe38c1mb1niacv.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"To determine the most acidic hydrogen, consider the resonance stability of the conjugate base. Greater the resonance delolalization, stronger the acidity. Acidic hydrogen is easily removed (as <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.129ex\" height=\"1.754ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 1383.1 775.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"48\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-48\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(783,363) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) and get conjugate base. The more stable the conjugate base, the more acidic the hydrogen.<div></div>\nIn option (B), the removal of the hydrogen leads to a carbanion which is resonance stabilized by conjugation with two adjacent double bonds. It is an allylic anion extended over a conjugated cyclic system.<div></div>In options (A), (C) and (D), allylic positions are present. But the resonance stabilization is less extensive compared to (B). Also, (A) and (C) are sterically hindered or less effectively delocalized.<div></div>In (B), removing the proton from the carbon adjacent to two double bonds. gives a conjugate base that can delocalize the negative charge over a five -carbon conjugated system (cyclopentadienyl-like system), which has aromatic stabilization when conjugated.\n\nMost acidic H is (B).<div></div>\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mbrp4sit/c11e74d5-05b1-4350-ace0-376de614729c/3bcc6240-469f-11f0-8bdf-c928f436ae39/file-jaoe38c1mbrp4siu.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1mbrp4sit/c11e74d5-05b1-4350-ace0-376de614729c/3bcc6240-469f-11f0-8bdf-c928f436ae39/file-jaoe38c1mbrp4siu.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2025 Paper 1 Online Chemistry - Hydrocarbons Question 5 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1mbrp4sit/c11e74d5-05b1-4350-ace0-376de614729c/3bcc6240-469f-11f0-8bdf-c928f436ae39/file-jaoe38c1mbrp4siu.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1mbrp4sit/c11e74d5-05b1-4350-ace0-376de614729c/3bcc6240-469f-11f0-8bdf-c928f436ae39/file-jaoe38c1mbrp4siu.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1mbrp4sit/c11e74d5-05b1-4350-ace0-376de614729c/3bcc6240-469f-11f0-8bdf-c928f436ae39/file-jaoe38c1mbrp4siu.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1mbrp4sit/c11e74d5-05b1-4350-ace0-376de614729c/3bcc6240-469f-11f0-8bdf-c928f436ae39/file-jaoe38c1mbrp4siu.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1mbrp4sit/c11e74d5-05b1-4350-ace0-376de614729c/3bcc6240-469f-11f0-8bdf-c928f436ae39/file-jaoe38c1mbrp4siu.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1mbrp4sit/c11e74d5-05b1-4350-ace0-376de614729c/3bcc6240-469f-11f0-8bdf-c928f436ae39/file-jaoe38c1mbrp4siu.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"><div></div>B forms most stable conjugate base and hence <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.717ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 759 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g str